1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:04,245
Native Foundation is a separate planning and controlled-adapter lane.

2
00:00:04,608 --> 00:00:08,661
Do not confuse it with the classic Foundation V M deployment workflow used

3
00:00:08,747 --> 00:00:09,941
elsewhere in this series.

4
00:00:10,197 --> 00:00:14,399
Inspect its returned read-only state, adapter readiness and blockers.

5
00:00:14,719 --> 00:00:18,261
A long list of successful review artifacts does not mean that physical

6
00:00:18,474 --> 00:00:20,884
imaging or cluster formation has taken place.

7
00:00:21,266 --> 00:00:24,850
A hardware probe can test selected connectivity and authentication

8
00:00:25,021 --> 00:00:25,703
conditions.

9
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,922
Read each result and its scope.

10
00:00:28,221 --> 00:00:31,591
A passed count can represent checks rather than the number of configured

11
00:00:31,634 --> 00:00:32,287
nodes.

12
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:36,737
Review manifests, provider operations, missing evidence and enabled

13
00:00:36,823 --> 00:00:38,508
execution flags separately.

14
00:00:38,871 --> 00:00:43,052
Evidence records, reservation plans and authorization reviews do not

15
00:00:43,095 --> 00:00:46,344
themselves prove that a deployment was admitted or executed.

16
00:00:46,869 --> 00:00:51,413
The post-foundation baseline workflows classify controls as apply, evidence,

17
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:52,949
manual or blocked.

18
00:00:53,183 --> 00:00:55,530
Only verified apply mappings execute.

19
00:00:55,743 --> 00:00:58,188
Evidence-only records capture observations.

20
00:00:58,584 --> 00:01:02,382
Manual controls still require a supported target procedure and retained

21
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:03,086
proof.

22
00:01:03,448 --> 00:01:05,659
Blocked controls need their gate resolved.

23
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:10,153
A successful overall job does not mean that every requested security,

24
00:01:10,473 --> 00:01:13,868
monitoring, network or certificate setting was changed.

25
00:01:14,345 --> 00:01:18,633
For hardware out-of-band access, controller credentials and certificates,

26
00:01:18,911 --> 00:01:22,559
confirm the supported platform procedure and your recovery path.

27
00:01:22,836 --> 00:01:26,377
Inspect any manual follow-up rather than treating an acknowledgement as

28
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,204
completion.

29
00:01:27,519 --> 00:01:30,805
Review independent target evidence for the controls that matter.

30
00:01:31,146 --> 00:01:33,834
Reconcile partial changes before retry.

31
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:38,101
Keep both the configuration intent and the actual verified result with the

32
00:01:38,143 --> 00:01:38,775
change record.

33
00:01:39,270 --> 00:01:44,049
Before enabling a specialist integration, verify its exact supported scope,

34
00:01:44,262 --> 00:01:47,462
keep approvals and preserve the original recovery path.

35
00:01:47,803 --> 00:01:51,942
Use the established Foundation V M and post-configuration workflows for the

36
00:01:51,984 --> 00:01:53,249
core cluster tasks.

37
00:01:53,532 --> 00:01:56,455
Check actual target state before accepting a change.

38
00:01:56,775 --> 00:01:59,926
Open Overview when you are ready to choose your next task.
